  "customfield_10154": null,
  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "$FEDORA_HOME/sever/config/config-melcoe-pep-mapping.xml specifies a mapping between the full set of API methods/action identifiers used for Fedora API operations and simplified versions of create, read, update, delete, admin",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Whilst this is useful for simplified authoring of policies; it has two deficiences:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "The simplified values are presented using the same Action attribute ID as the standard Fedora Action attribute ID - which is misleading/confusing (these simplified values should be a separate attribute ID?)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "The original Fedora action IDs are not retained, making it difficult to write granular policies.  For example it's not easy to distinguish between purging an object and purging a datastream, as the same action ID is supplied (in fact the only way currently is to look at the full resource ID and see if there's a datastream on the end, which is not very useful).",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So suggeste action would be:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1) The simplified action IDs should be presented using a different a different action attribute ID",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) The original Fedora action IDs should be retained, for more granular-level policies",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "But:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1) is a breaking change; any existing policies based on these simplified action IDs would break.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So a compromise would be to present both the fedora-original and FeSL-simplified action IDs using the same attribute ID; as the simplified values don't collide with the existing values.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Example:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Attribute ID:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "urn:fedora:names:fedora:2.1:action:id",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Value:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "urn:fedora:names:fedora:2.1:action:id-purgeObject",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Is translated by FeSL, and presented to the PDP as:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Attribute ID:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "urn:fedora:names:fedora:2.1:action:id",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Value:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "delete",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(note that the original, granular method-level value is not retained).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There is a kind of work-around currently which is to amend the mappings back to their original values; but this means you loose the simplified attributes, so is only a work-around for specific situations.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
