      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Actually, including both the existing granular action attributes and the fesl simplified ones using the same attribute ID may not be entirely correct; as this attribute may be single-valued (and this would instead make it a bag; might break existing policies in other ways).</p>\n\n<p>Although... everything is treated as a bag.  But we do have the scenario where a resource attribute that had one-and-only-one value would now have two - could this have an impact?</p>",
     "created": "07/Feb/12 4:00 PM",
     "id": "12230",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11025/comment/12230",
